# plane-cli

A lightweight CLI tool for interacting with your [Plane](https://plane.so) instance.

## Installation

### From Source

```bash
git clone https://github.com/plane-cli/plane-cli.git
cd plane-cli
make build      # outputs ./plane binary
make install    # installs to $GOPATH/bin
```

### From Release

Download the pre-built binary for your platform from the [Releases](https://github.com/plane-cli/plane-cli/releases) page.

Available platforms: Linux, macOS, Windows (amd64, arm64)

## Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Initialize configuration
plane config init

# 2. Verify connection
plane user me

# 3. List projects
plane project list -w my-workspace

# 4. List issues
plane issue list -w my-workspace -p <project-id>
```

## Configuration

Config file location: `~/.config/plane-cli/config.yaml`

```bash
plane config init                        # Interactive setup
plane config set workspace my-workspace  # Set a value
plane config get workspace               # Get a value
plane config list                        # Show all values (API key masked)
```

### Config Keys

| Key | Description | Env Variable |
|-----|-------------|--------------|
| `base_url` | Plane instance URL | `PLANE_BASE_URL` |
| `api_key` | API key for authentication | `PLANE_API_KEY` |
| `workspace` | Default workspace slug | `PLANE_WORKSPACE` |
| `project` | Default project ID | `PLANE_PROJECT` |
| `format` | Output format (`json` or `table`) | `PLANE_FORMAT` |

**Priority**: CLI flags > Environment variables > Config file

## Global Flags

```
-w, --workspace string   Workspace slug
-p, --project string     Project ID
-f, --format string      Output format: json, table (default: json)
-q, --quiet              Suppress non-error output
    --debug              Enable HTTP request/response logging
    --base-url string    API base URL override
    --config string      Config file path
```

## Commands

### User

```bash
plane user me    # Show current authenticated user
```

### Project (alias: `proj`)

Requires: `--workspace`

```bash
plane project list
plane project get <project-id>
plane project create --name "My Project" --identifier "MP" [--description "..."] [--network 0|2]
plane project update <project-id> [--name "..."] [--description "..."]
plane project delete <project-id>
```

### Issue (alias: `i`)

Requires: `--workspace`, `--project`

Issues can be referenced by UUID or identifier format (e.g., `PROJ-123`).

```bash
# List & Search
plane issue list [--state <id>] [--priority urgent|high|medium|low|none] [--assignee <id>] [--per-page 100] [--cursor <cursor>]
plane issue search --query "search text"
plane issue get <issue-id-or-PROJ-123>
plane issue get-by-seq <sequence-number>

# Create
plane issue create --name "Bug fix" \
  [--description "<p>HTML content</p>"] \
  [--state <state-id>] \
  [--priority urgent|high|medium|low|none] \
  [--assignee <user-id>] \
  [--label <label-id>] \
  [--parent <issue-id>] \
  [--start-date 2024-01-01] \
  [--target-date 2024-01-31]

# Update & Delete
plane issue update <issue-id-or-PROJ-123> [--name "..."] [--state <id>] [--priority <p>]
plane issue delete <issue-id-or-PROJ-123>
```

`--assignee` and `--label` flags accept comma-separated values or can be repeated:
```bash
plane issue create --name "Task" --assignee id1 --assignee id2
plane issue create --name "Task" --label "id1,id2"
```

